{
  "format": 1,
  "id": "slope-intercept",
  "title": "Slope and intercept",
  "summary": "How m and b move a line.",
  "level": "core",
  "minutes": 7,
  "outcomes": [
    "o1",
    "o2"
  ],
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "motivate",
      "html": "<p>A phone plan costs a fixed amount plus a price per gigabyte. Which number changes the bill more when you use more data?</p>"
    },
    {
      "type": "predict",
      "id": "si-p0",
      "prompt": "Plan A costs 10 plus 2 per GB. Plan B costs 20 plus 1 per GB. At 15 GB, which plan is cheaper?",
      "options": [
        "Plan A",
        "Plan B",
        "They cost the same"
      ],
      "correct": 1,
      "feedback": {
        "0": "Plan A starts cheaper, but its price per GB is higher. At 15 GB it costs 10 + 30 = 40, while Plan B costs 20 + 15 = 35.",
        "2": "They cost the same only at 10 GB (30 each). At 15 GB, the per-GB price has made Plan A more expensive."
      },
      "explanation": "Plan A: 10 + 2·15 = 40. Plan B: 20 + 1·15 = 35. With enough data, the per-GB price matters more than the fixed amount."
    },
    {
      "type": "visual",
      "purpose": "Show slope and intercept on one line",
      "alt": "A straight line crossing the vertical axis at b and rising m units for every unit to the right.",
      "html": "<figure><svg viewBox='0 0 300 120' role='img' aria-label='Line with slope and intercept'><line class='edge' x1='20' y1='100' x2='280' y2='20'/><text class='ts' x='24' y='96'>b</text><text class='ts' x='200' y='60'>m</text></svg><figcaption>y = m·x + b</figcaption></figure>"
    },
    {
      "type": "explain",
      "html": "<p>In y = m·x + b, the <span class='term' data-term='slope'>slope</span> m is the change in y per unit of x and the <span class='term' data-term='intercept'>intercept</span> b is the value at x = 0.</p>"
    },
    {
      "type": "worked",
      "steps": [
        {
          "html": "<p>y = 2x + 1 at x = 3: 2·3 = 6.</p>"
        },
        {
          "html": "<p>6 + 1 = 7.</p>"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "activity",
      "id": "lab1",
      "widget": "function-lab",
      "concepts": [
        "slope",
        "intercept",
        "check-models"
      ],
      "instructions": "<p>Predict first, then move the slider.</p>",
      "debrief": "<p>The slope tilts the line; the intercept shifts it.</p>",
      "config": {
        "title": "Slope and intercept lab",
        "params": [
          {
            "id": "m",
            "label": "slope m",
            "min": -3,
            "max": 3,
            "step": 0.5,
            "value": 1
          },
          {
            "id": "b",
            "label": "intercept b",
            "min": -4,
            "max": 4,
            "step": 1,
            "value": 0
          }
        ],
        "x": {
          "from": -5,
          "to": 5,
          "label": "x"
        },
        "y": {
          "from": -10,
          "to": 10
        },
        "curves": [
          {
            "label": "y = m·x + b",
            "expr": "m*x + b"
          }
        ],
        "readouts": [
          {
            "label": "y at x = 2",
            "expr": "m*2 + b"
          },
          {
            "label": "y at x = 0",
            "expr": "b"
          }
        ],
        "markers": [
          {
            "label": "(2, y)",
            "x": "2",
            "y": "m*2 + b"
          }
        ],
        "tasks": [
          {
            "id": "t1",
            "type": "direction",
            "prompt": "If you increase the slope m, what happens to y at x = 2?",
            "param": "m",
            "watch": "m*2 + b",
            "explanation": "<p>At x = 2 the output is 2m + b, so it rises by 2 for every unit of m.</p>"
          },
          {
            "id": "t2",
            "type": "direction",
            "prompt": "If you increase the intercept b, what happens to y at x = 2?",
            "param": "b",
            "watch": "m*2 + b",
            "explanation": "<p>b shifts every point of the line up by the same amount.</p>"
          },
          {
            "id": "t3",
            "type": "value",
            "prompt": "With m = 2 and b = -1, what is y at x = 3?",
            "set": {
              "m": 2,
              "b": -1
            },
            "expr": "m*3 + b",
            "tolerance": 0.001,
            "explanation": "<p>2·3 − 1 = 5.</p>"
          }
        ],
        "testCases": [
          {
            "label": "y(3) with m=2, b=-1",
            "set": {
              "m": 2,
              "b": -1
            },
            "expr": "m*3 + b",
            "value": 5
          },
          {
            "label": "intercept",
            "set": {
              "m": 7,
              "b": 3
            },
            "expr": "m*0 + b",
            "value": 3
          }
        ],
        "limitPrompt": "State one situation where a straight line would be a poor model.",
        "limitModel": "<p>Growth that speeds up (compound interest), or quantities with a ceiling.</p>",
        "assumptions": [
          "Pure linear model y = m·x + b",
          "Inputs between −5 and 5 only"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "practice",
      "id": "p1",
      "level": "guided",
      "task": "<p>Compute y for y = 3x − 2 at x = 4.</p>",
      "hints": [
        "<p>Multiply first.</p>"
      ],
      "solution": "<p>10</p>",
      "concepts": [
        "evaluate-linear"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "practice",
      "id": "p2",
      "level": "independent",
      "setting": "real-world",
      "externalFeedback": "<p>Ask someone to check one value of your bill model against a real bill.</p>",
      "task": "<p>Model one of your own bills as a line and check one value.</p>",
      "rubric": [
        "States m and b",
        "Checks one value"
      ],
      "solution": "<p>Answers vary.</p>",
      "concepts": [
        "check-models"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "check",
      "questions": [
        {
          "id": "c1",
          "assesses": [
            "o1"
          ],
          "concepts": [
            "slope"
          ],
          "prompt": "Increasing m makes the line…",
          "options": [
            "steeper (if m > 0)",
            "move up without tilting"
          ],
          "correct": 0,
          "explanation": "m controls the tilt.",
          "feedback": {
            "1": "That is what b does."
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "c2",
          "assesses": [
            "o2"
          ],
          "concepts": [
            "evaluate-linear",
            "intercept"
          ],
          "kind": "numeric",
          "prompt": "y = 2x + 3 at x = 0?",
          "answer": 3,
          "tolerance": 0,
          "explanation": "At x = 0 the output is b.",
          "feedbackWrong": "At x = 0 the slope term vanishes."
        },
        {
          "id": "c3",
          "assesses": [
            "o1"
          ],
          "concepts": [
            "rate-of-change"
          ],
          "kind": "open",
          "prompt": "Explain slope as a rate of change in your own words.",
          "rubric": [
            "Mentions change per unit"
          ],
          "model": "<p>The output changes by m for each unit of input.</p>"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "transfer",
      "id": "tr1",
      "assesses": [
        "o1",
        "o2"
      ],
      "concepts": [
        "rate-of-change"
      ],
      "task": "<p>A plant grows 2 cm per week from 5 cm. Model it and predict week 6.</p>",
      "rubric": [
        "y = 2x + 5",
        "17 cm"
      ],
      "model": "<p>y = 2·6 + 5 = 17 cm.</p>"
    }
  ],
  "sources": [
